Got it 👍 — right now your Apex is still pushing a **single big text blob** into `res.result`. That’s why the agent keeps echoing raw strings instead of giving you the polished, conversational table you want.

If you want the **agent to automatically re-render into a Markdown table (with summary, insights, follow-ups)**, you should not flatten the SOQL results into a text table in Apex. Instead, return a **structured DTO list** (rows of customer, orders, revenue). Then your Topic instructions can say: “Always render structured records as markdown tables + conversational summary.”

---

## ✅ Refactored Apex (Structured Output DTO)

```apex
public with sharing class Customer_TopRevenueAction {

    public class Request {
        @InvocableVariable(required=false)
        public Integer limitSize;
    }

    public class Response {
        @InvocableVariable(label='Customer')
        public String customer;

        @InvocableVariable(label='Orders')
        public Integer orders;

        @InvocableVariable(label='Total Revenue')
        public Decimal totalRevenue;
    }

    @InvocableMethod(label='Top Revenue Customers' description='List top customers by revenue')
    public static List<Response> run(List<Request> reqs) {
        Integer limitValue = 10;
        if (reqs != null && !reqs.isEmpty() && reqs[0].limitSize != null && reqs[0].limitSize > 0) {
            limitValue = reqs[0].limitSize;
        }

        List<Response> results = new List<Response>();

        for (AggregateResult ar : [
            SELECT CustomerName__c custName,
                   COUNT(Id) orderCount,
                   SUM(Revenue__c) sumRevenue
            FROM Realistic_OrderLine_Datacsv__dlm
            GROUP BY CustomerName__c
            ORDER BY SUM(Revenue__c) DESC
            LIMIT :limitValue
        ]) {
            Response r = new Response();
            r.customer = (String) ar.get('custName');
            r.orders = (Integer) ar.get('orderCount');
            r.totalRevenue = (Decimal) ar.get('sumRevenue');
            results.add(r);
        }

        return results;
    }
}
```

---

## 🔑 Why this is better

* Instead of sending `"Customer | Orders | Total Revenue..."` text → you send **structured records** (`customer`, `orders`, `totalRevenue`).
* Your Topic instructions can now say:

```
Always take the structured records (Customer, Orders, Revenue) 
and display them as a markdown table with conversational summary, 
insights, and follow-ups. Never echo raw JSON.
```

